__NUXT_JSONP__("/tr/testimonials", (function(a,b,c,d,e,f,g,h,i,j,k,l,m,n,o,p){return {data:[{details:{slug:k,pageTitle:"Öğrenci tanıklıkları | Mentor Language Institute",pageDescription:"Comments about MLI from students.",title:"Öğrenci tanıklıkları",selectBy:{title:"Seçmek için:",selections:[{title:"Nationality",key:"nationality",lists:[{title:"All Nationalities",value:l},{image:"\u002Fflags\u002Fsa.png",title:g,link:"ar"},{image:"\u002Fflags\u002Fkr.png",title:h,link:"kr"},{image:"\u002Fflags\u002Fru.png",title:i,link:"ru"},{image:"\u002Fflags\u002Ffr.png",title:j,link:"fr"},{image:"\u002Fflags\u002Fes.png",title:m,link:"sp"},{image:"\u002Fflags\u002Fth.png",title:"Thai",link:"th"},{image:"\u002Fflags\u002Fjp.png",title:c,link:"jp"},{image:"\u002Fflags\u002Fbr.png",title:f,link:"por"},{image:"\u002Fflags\u002Fcn.png",title:e,link:"ch"},{image:"\u002Fflags\u002Fit.png",title:o,link:"it"},{image:"\u002Fflags\u002Ftr.png",title:n,link:k},{image:"\u002Fflags\u002Fde.png",title:"German",link:"de"},{image:"\u002Fflags\u002Fother.png",title:d,link:l}]},{title:p,key:"campus",lists:[{title:p,value:l},{title:"Westwood",image:"\u002Fcampus\u002Fwestwood.png"},{title:"Hollywood",image:"\u002Fcampus\u002Fhollywood.png"}]}]},comments:{title:" Comments about MLI from students."},readmoreBtn:"Daha fazla oku",dir:"\u002Ftestimonials",path:"\u002Ftestimonials\u002Ftr",extension:".json",createdAt:"2026-10-22T16:31:31.224Z",updatedAt:"2025-05-26T12:06:27.938Z"},lang:k,allTestimonials:[{id:90,image:"1761607523-ee42a2a8-83ba-4873-9cbf-df2be365d5cc.JPG",campus_name:a,nationality_name:n,title:"BENIM MLI MACERAM",text:"Merhaba, ben Merve. Turkiye’den MLI’da altı aylık bir İngilizce kursuna katıldım ve gerçekten\nhayatımın en güzel deneyimlerinden biriydi. Farklı kültürlerden birçok harika insanla tanıştım ve\nprofesyonel öğretmenlerle çalışma fırsatı buldum. Her ders çok keyifliydi.\n\nLos Angeles’ı seçtim çünkü yeni insanlarla tanışmak ve kültürel değişim yaşamak için harika bir yer.\n\nMLI’a ilk başladığımda İngilizceyi pek iyi konuşamıyordum. Kendime güvenim yoktu ve konuşmaya çalıştığımda çok heyecanlanıyordum. Ama birkaç ay sonra her şey değişti daha çok konuşmaya başladım, özgüvenim geldi ve dışarıda tek başıma birçok şeyi yapabildiğimi fark ettim.\nŞimdi çok daha iyi konuşabiliyorum, bunun için sınıfıma minnettarım.\n\nMLI’daki her anım benim için unutulmazdı ama bir tanesi benim için özel. Hep birlikte Pacific.\nPark’a barbekü yapmaya gittik. Harikaydı! Barbekü yedik, voleybol oynadık ve birçok eğlenceli sohbet ettik.\n\nGelecekteki planım ABD’de mühendis olarak çalışmak. İşimde İngilizce kullanarak ve her gün kendimi geliştirmek istiyorum."},{id:89,image:"1750786714-Gahyun Kim.JPG",campus_name:b,nationality_name:h,title:"Los Angeles’taki EN İYİ Anım",text:"Merhaba! Benim adım Lily ve Güney Kore’den geliyorum. Ocak’tan Mart’a kadar MLI’da eğitim gördüm. Hep Los Angeles ve Hollywood’da yaşamayı hayal ettim, bu yüzden MLI’yı seçtim; en büyük sebebi Hollywood’un ana caddesinde yer almasıydı! Okuldan çıkıp Hollywood’un tam kalbinde olmak gerçekten eğlenceli ve heyecan vericiydi.\n\nNeden Los Angeles?\nLA’yı seçmemin nedeni, yapılacak çok şeyle dolu bir şehir olduğunu düşünmemdi—ve haklıymışım! Yakınlarda plajlar ve dağlar var ve Santa Monica, Griffith Gözlemevi ve Getty Center gibi yerleri keşfetmeyi çok sevdim. Her hafta sonu yeni bir macera gibiydi.\n\nMLI’da İngilizce Gelişimi ve Sınıf Deneyimi\nMLI’da tüm dünyadan öğrencilerin olduğu bir sınıftaydım, bu da İngilizcemi doğal olarak geliştirmeme gerçekten yardımcı oldu. Her gün konuşma pratiği yapıyorduk ve öğretmenlerimiz ile sınıf arkadaşlarım sayesinde farklı durumlarda İngilizce kullanma konusunda daha fazla özgüven kazandım. Dilbilgisi, iletişim ve iş İngilizcesi dersleri aldım.\nAyrıca, MLI personeli her zaman çok nazik ve destekleyiciydi. Sınıf içinde ve dışında ne olursa olsun her konuda yardımcı olmaktan mutluydular, bu da orada bulunduğum süre boyunca kendimi çok rahat ve hoş karşılanmış hissetmemi sağladı.\n\nUnutulmaz An\nMLI'daki en sevdiğim kısmı etkinliklerin çeşitliliğiydi. Las Vegas gezisine, barbekü partisinde ve Disneyland gününe katıldım ve hepsi unutulmazdı! Bu anları gerçekten özel kılan şey, yalnızca diğer Koreli öğrencilerle değil, uluslararası arkadaşlarla da vakit geçirebilmemdi. Bu aktiviteler bize bağ kurMA şansı tanıdı ve birçoğumuz okul dışında da birlikte takılmaya devam ettik.\n\nGelecek Planı\nŞu anda LA’de çocuklar için bir kar amacı gütmeyen kuruluşta staj yapıyorum. Planım burada deneyim kazanmaya devam etmek ve umarım bu alanda çalışmaya devam etmek. Bu şehirde öğrenmeye ve büyümeye devam etmeyi dört gözle bekliyorum. Ve MLI’da yaşadığım anının LA’daki EN İYİ anım olduğuna kesinlikle eminim!"},{id:88,image:"1744833045-Testimonials _Yoonbin.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:e,title:"ABD’deki İlk Dil Okulu ve Staj Deneyimim",text:"Merhaba! Ben Yoonbin Bae, Güney Koreliyim. Kısa bir süre önce MLI’deki dil kursumu tamamladım ve şu anda bir staj programına katılıyorum. MLI’de geçirdiğim süre boyunca farklı kültürel geçmişlere sahip insanlarla etkileşim kurma fırsatı buldum ve İngilizce becerilerimi geliştirdim. İleri Seviye Sınıfında, İngilizceyi daha doğru ifade etmeyi öğrendim, daha doğal bir konuşma tarzı geliştirdim ve eleştirel düşünme yeteneğimi güçlendirdim. Gelişmiş konuşma çalışmaları, akademik makale yazımı ve analitik okuma alıştırmaları sayesinde çok değerli bir eğitim deneyimi yaşadım.\n\n- Neden Los Angeles?\n\nLos Angeles’ı seçmemin nedeni bu şehirle özel bir bağımın olmasıydı. On yıl önce, ilkokul ve ortaokulu Los Angeles’ta okudum ve burada İngilizce temelimi sağlamlaştırırken farklı geçmişlere sahip insanlarla harika anılar biriktirdim. Bu değerli deneyimler beni ABD’ye geri dönmeye teşvik etti. Ayrıca, Los Angeles’ın mükemmel iklimi ve sıcak insanları burayı İngilizcemi geliştirmek için ideal bir yer haline getirdi.\n\n- İngilizce Gelişimim\n\nMLI’de eğitim almak kesinlikle İngilizce becerilerimi geliştirdi. Temel bilgim olmasına rağmen, uzun süre pratik yapmadığım için kendimi akıcı bir şekilde ifade etmekte zorlanıyordum. Ancak, özverili eğitmenlerimin desteği sayesinde düşüncelerimi daha doğru ve doğrudan aktarma konusunda güven kazandım.\n\n- En Unutulmaz Anım\n\nMLI’deki birçok aktivite arasından en unutulmaz deneyimim Las Vegas gezisiydi. Üç gün ve iki gece boyunca arkadaşlarımla birlikte farklı ülkeleri temsil eden otelleri keşfettik, parlak neon ışıkları altında sayısız fotoğraf çektik ve ünlü Bellagio çeşme gösterisinin keyfini çıkardık. Ayrıca, 10 saat süren bir otobüs yolculuğuyla muhteşem Grand Canyon’u ziyaret ettik. Bu harika anları MLI’deki arkadaşlarımla paylaşmak deneyimi daha da özel kıldı ve bu anıları sonsuza dek saklayacağım.\n\n- Gelecek Planlarım\n\nŞu anda en büyük önceliğim ABD’deki stajımı tamamlamak. Daha sonra, geliştirdiğim İngilizce becerilerimi ve staj sırasında kazandığım pazarlama bilgimi kullanarak yurt dışında çok uluslu bir şirkette çalışmayı hedefliyorum. MLI’de geçirdiğim zaman bana güven ve daha geniş bir bakış açısı kazandırdı, böylece küresel bir iş ortamında başarılı olabilmek için gerekli hazırlıkları yapmış oldum.\n\nMLI’deki deneyimim sadece İngilizce öğrenmekten ibaret değildi, aynı zamanda büyüme ve keşif dolu, paha biçilemez bir yolculuktu. Dünyanın dört bir yanından gelen arkadaşlarla anlamlı etkileşimler kurarak ufkumu genişlettim ve hayallerime ulaşma yolunda ilk adımımı attım. Teşekkürler, MLI!"},{id:87,image:"1743099948-IMG_9244.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:h,title:"MLI’DEKİ EN HARİKA DENEYİMİM!",text:"Merhaba, benim adım Seohyun Shin ve Koreliyim. MLI’de yaklaşık iki ay geçirdim ve orada yaşadığım deneyim gerçekten çok değerli ve keyifliydi. Daha uzun süre kalmak isterdim ama maalesef yaklaşan staj programım nedeniyle erken mezun olmak zorunda kaldım, bu da beni çok üzdü. Şimdi, neden MLI’deki deneyimimi “en harika deneyim” olarak adlandırdığımı size anlatmak istiyorum!\n\n◉Neden Los Angeles?\nİngilizce eğitimim için Los Angeles'ı seçmek hayatımda verdiğim en iyi kararlardan biriydi. Los Angeles farklı kültürlerin bir araya geldiği bir şehir ve burada eğitim almanın bana dünyanın dört bir yanından insanlarla tanışma fırsatı vereceğini biliyordum. Şehrin hareketli atmosferi, farklı toplulukları ve günlük hayatta İngilizce pratiği yapma imkânları, dil becerilerimi geliştirmek için mükemmel bir ortam sundu. Hollywood Walk of Fame'i keşfetmekten Santa Monica’da güneşli günlerin tadını çıkarmaya kadar Los Angeles’taki her günüm, öğrenme deneyimime katkıda bulunan bir macera oldu.\n\n◉İngilizce gelişimim\nMLI’de geçirdiğim süre boyunca okuma, dinleme ve dil bilgisi becerilerimde önemli gelişmeler kaydettim. Özellikle İş İngilizcesi dersleri çok faydalı oldu ve profesyonel ortamlarda etkili bir şekilde iletişim kurma konusunda bana güven kazandırdı. Eğitmenler inanılmaz derecede destekleyiciydi ve etkileşimli dersler, karmaşık dil bilgisi kurallarını daha iyi anlamama ve dinleme becerimi geliştirmeme yardımcı oldu. Sınıf arkadaşlarımla veya Los Angeles’taki günlük yaşamda konuşurken kendimi daha rahat ve akıcı hissettiğimi fark ettim.\n\n◉Unutulmaz anım\nMLI’deki en unutulmaz anlardan biri, üç günlük Las Vegas gezisiydi. Sınıf arkadaşlarımla birlikte seyahat etmek, şehrin parlak ışıklarını görmek ve canlı atmosferi deneyimlemek unutulmaz anılar yarattı. Barbekü partisi ve Disneyland gezisi de en güzel anılardan bazılarıydı — farklı ülkelerden arkadaşlarla birlikte lezzetli yemekler yemek ve heyecan verici oyunlara katılmak aramızda güçlü bir bağ oluşturdu. Ay Yeni Yılı ve Sevgililer Günü gibi kültürel etkinlikleri kutlamak, MLI topluluğuna bağlılık hissi yarattı ve bu hissi hep yanımda taşıyacağım.\n\n◉Gelecek planlarım\nMLI’deki deneyimim bana gelecekteki hedeflerimi gerçekleştirmem için güven ve beceri kazandırdı. İş İngilizcesi dersleri ve gelişmiş iletişim becerilerim sayesinde artık stajıma başlamak ve uluslararası bir ortamda çalışmak için daha hazır hissediyorum. MLI’de öğrendiklerimi gelecekteki kariyerimde uygulamak için sabırsızlanıyorum ve burada kurduğum dostlukların ve yaşadığım deneyimlerin hayatım boyunca benimle kalacağını biliyorum."},{id:86,image:"1739488748-Testimonials_Yuka.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:c,title:"Son 10 ayın değerli anıları",text:"Adım Yuka, Japonya'dan geliyorum. 8 aydır MLI'de eğitim alıyorum çünkü iyi bir İngilizce konuşmak ve çok sayıda arkadaş edinmek istiyorum. Bu okul aracılığıyla harika öğretmenlerle tanıştım ve çok güzel arkadaşlar edindim. Burada geçirdiğim zaman, bana unutulmaz anılar ve deneyimler kazandırdı.\n\nNeden Los Angeles?\nEşim 7 yıldır Los Angeles'ta yaşıyor. Bir buçuk yıl önce evlendik ve 8 ay önce onunla birlikte olmak için buraya geldim. Ortaokuldayken birkaç günlüğüne Los Angeles’a gelmiştim. Bu, en tatlı anılarımdan biri, ancak burada yaşayacağımı hiç düşünmemiştim.\n\nİngilizce gelişimim\nBir yıl önce, restoranlarda sipariş verirken veya Amerikalı arkadaşlarımla konuşurken eşimin çevirisine güveniyordum, ancak son zamanlarda yavaş yavaş sipariş verebiliyor veya kendi başıma konuşabiliyorum. Konuşma becerim kadar yazma becerim de gelişti çünkü İngilizce bir günlük yazma ödevim var.\n\nLos Angeles'taki unutulmaz anım\nHer yıl 4 Temmuz, Amerika Birleşik Devletleri'nde Bağımsızlık Günü’dür ve bu, Noel ve Cadılar Bayramı kadar önemli ve büyük bir tatildir. ABD'nin birçok eyaletinde havai fişekler için kısıtlamalar olduğu söyleniyor, ancak bu günde özel olarak izin veriliyor.\nO gün arkadaşlarımın evine gittim. Evlendikleri bina 20 katlı ve gece çatı katından havai fişekleri izledik. Görüş açımız tamamen açıktı ve baktığımız her yerde güzel havai fişekler görebiliyorduk! Japonya’da havai fişekler yazın önemli bir özelliğidir ve birçok kez gördüm, ancak böyle bir deneyimim hiç olmamıştı.\n\nGelecek planlarım\nAslında burada daha uzun süre kalmayı planlıyordum, ancak bazı sebeplerden dolayı gelecek ay eşimle birlikte Japonya'ya dönmem gerekiyor. Bu yüzden programımı, haftada en az bir veya iki kez İngilizce konuşma dersine katılacak şekilde ayarlamayı planlıyorum. Bir gün yine ailemle yurtdışında yaşamayı çok isterim. Bunun çok uzun sürmeyeceğini düşünüyorum."},{id:85,image:"1739488466-IMG_0528.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:d,title:"MLI, LOS ANGELES'İN EN İYİ BÜYÜKELÇİSİDİR",text:"Adım Gloria, Kolombiya'dan geliyorum. MLI ile ilk iletişime geçtiğim andan itibaren, resepsiyon personelinin nazikliği sayesinde harika bir deneyim oldu. Hemen buranın İngilizce öğrenmek için mükemmel okul olduğunu fark ettim.\n\nO dönemde Massachusetts, Boston'da yaşıyordum ve Los Angeles'a taşınmaya karar verdim çünkü benim için çok önemli olan üç neden vardı:\n\nLos Angeles, dört mevsimde de en iyi havaya sahip, Medellin, doğduğum şehir gibi.\nLos Angeles, eğlencenin başkenti ve okul, her hafta turistlik yerleri gezmek için çok kapsamlı aktiviteler sunuyor.\nDiğer ülkelerden gelen insanlarla vakit geçirebiliyorum. Kültürlerini öğrenmek beni heyecanlandırıyor ve gelecekte onları ziyaret etmeyi planlıyorum.\nBenim zorluğum, İngilizceyi akıcı bir şekilde konuşmak ve MLI'deki tüm öğretmenlerin öğretmek için tutku, sevgi ve sabırla yaklaştıklarını görmek beni çok etkiliyor. Bunu başaracağımı temin ederim.\n\nMLI'deki en güzel anım Venice Beach'teki yaz etkinliği oldu. Hollywood kampüsü ve Westwood kampüsündeki öğretmenler ve öğrencilerle harika zaman geçirdim. Kusursuz organizasyon, lezzetli yemekler ve eğlenceli oyunlar o günü unutulmaz kıldı.\n\nMLI'deki eğitimimi tamamladıktan sonra, Los Angeles'ta Otelcilik Yönetimi okumaya devam etmek ve global bir otel zincirinde otel sektöründe çalışmaya devam etmek istiyorum."},{id:84,image:"1739488177-IMG_3762.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:d,title:"Öğrenmek, Bağlanmak ve Keşfetmek: MLI'deki Hayatım Los Angeles'ta",text:"Adım Lesli ve Meksika'dan geliyorum. Los Angeles'ta iki yıldır yaşıyorum ve MLI'de İngilizce öğrenip bu şehrin farklı kültürlerini keşfetmek için eğitim alıyorum.\n\nBence MLI, Los Angeles'ta İngilizce öğrenmek için harika bir yer. Ortam sıcak ve pozitif, bu da kendimi evimde gibi hissettirdi. Deneyimimin en öne çıkan noktalarından biri, öğretmenler ve personel tarafından gösterilen destek. En sevdiğim öğretmenim Tom, eğitim yolculuğum boyunca son derece sabırlı ve teşvik edici oldu. Konuları tamamen anladığım kadarını defalarca açıkladı, bu da öğrenme süreci de köklü bir değişim sağladı.\n\nMLI'ye gelmeden önce, bu kadar farklı ülkelerden insanlarla tanışacağımı ve Asya ve Avrupa kültürleri hakkında bu kadar çok şey öğreneceğimi hayal etmemiştim. Ayrıca, sınıf arkadaşlarım ve personelle harika dostluklar kurdum, bu da buradaki zamanımı daha özel hale getirdi. Los Angeles, Orta ve Güney Amerika kültürleri hakkında daha fazla şey öğrenmek de yardımcı oldu ve bu, bakış açımı zenginleştirdi.\n\nLos Angeles'ta yaşamayı seçmemin birkaç nedeni vardı: İlk olarak, sıcak havası, ikinci olarak Meksika'ya yakın olması ve üçüncü olarak farklı kültürlerden gelen çeşitli yemekleri tatma fırsatıydı. Kırsal bir yerden geldiğim için büyük bir şehirde yaşamak heyecan verici bir macera oldu. Şehir ışıklarını geceleri seviyorum, dağların güzelliğine hayran kaldım ve burada ilk kez kar gördüm, bu gerçekten harikaydı!\n\nMLI'ye başladığımda, başlangıç seviyesindeyim ve şimdi, bir yıl sonra, ileri seviyeye geldim. Bu kolay bir yol değildi, ama her zorluk buna değerdi. Bir sonraki hedefim TOEFL hazırlık dersini almak."},{id:79,image:"1681173263-unnamed (1).jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:c,title:"Los Angeles'i Keşfetmek ve MLI'da İngilizce Becerilerini Geliştirmek",text:"Bu hafta, Japonya'dan yeni katılmış bir ESL başlangıç programı öğrencisi olan Myu'yu tanıtmaktan heyecan duyuyoruz. Myu, farklı dünya bölgelerinden diğer öğrencilerle İngilizce öğrenmeyi ve pratiğini yapmayı seviyor. Dil öğrenme tutkusunun yanı sıra, Myu yeni yerleri ve kültürleri keşfetmeye de büyük ilgi duyuyor.\n\n\"Bu okula bir hafta katıldım. İlk olarak test edilirsiniz ve size en uygun sınıfa yerleştirilirsiniz. O zamanlar yaklaşık 10 öğrenci vardı ve öğretmen ile öğrenciler arasındaki mesafe yakındı, bu yüzden dersin keyfini çıkarabildim. 'Sadece İngilizce öğretilir' prensibi altında, çeşitli ülkelerden sınıf arkadaşlarıyla telaffuz, dilbilgisi, konuşma ve daha fazlasını öğrenebilirsiniz. Okuldan sonra arkadaşlarımla Venice Beach'e gittim. Rahatlatıcı bir zaman geçirdik ve böyle harika bir manzara görerek çok keyifli bir zaman geçirdim. Sadece bir haftalık çok kısa bir yurt dışı öğrenimi olsa da, çeşitli ülkelerden sınıf arkadaşlarıyla derslerin keyfini çıkarabildim ve okuldan sonra arkadaşlarımla Los Angeles'ta gezintiye çıkarak unutulmaz bir zaman geçirdim. Bu kısa sürede bile yeni bir dünya görebildim, yeni arkadaşlar edinebildim ve bu çok değerli bir deneyimdi.\""},{id:78,image:"1678978291-1678926029-image1.jpeg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:c,title:"Los Angeles'taki Mentor Dil Okulu'ndaki Unutulmaz Zamanım",text:"Bu hafta, şu anda başlangıç programımıza kayıtlı olan Japonya'dan Kaima adlı öğrencimizi tanıtıyoruz. Kaima, uluslararası öğrencilerle konuşmaktan keyif alıyor ve Las Vegas ve LACMA gibi birçok yere seyahat etme fırsatı buldu ve bunları son derece keyifli buldu.\n\n\"Burada yaşam harika.\n\nMLI mükemmel bir okul. İngilizce öğrenmek istiyorsanız, burada sıkı çalışmayı şiddetle öneriyorum. MLI, ESL, TOEFL, Konuşma vb. gibi birçok İngilizce dersi sunar, bu nedenle seviyenize göre ders seçebilirsiniz. Ayrıca öğretmenler ve öğrenciler de dost canlısı olduğundan, ders gerçekten keyifli oluyor.\nOnlarla iletişim kurmak için her zaman İngilizce konuşmak gerekir, bu da dil pratiği için daha fazla fırsata neden olur. İngilizce öğreniyorum çünkü akıcı bir şekilde konuşabilmek istiyorum ve burada kalmak kesinlikle becerilerinizi geliştirecektir. Sadece üç haftada özellikle kelime dağarcığı açısından birçok yeni şey öğrendim ve konuşma yeteneklerimde önemli bir iyileşme görüyorum.\n\nAyrıca konum harika - Los Angeles, Hollywood ve Santa Monica Plajı gibi birçok turistik mekana sahip güzel bir şehir, burada birçok heyecan verici deneyim yaşayabilirsiniz. Eğer tereddüt ediyorsanız, gelmenizi öneriyorum - burada yaşam harika.\""},{id:76,image:"1678977545-1628060810-mathieu.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:j,title:"Neden Los Angeles\\'da Okumayı Seviyorum?",text:"Bu haftanin seçkin öğrencisi, Fransa\\'dan Mathieu. Evine döndüğünde, Nice, Fransa\\'da Finans veya Emlak üzerine odaklanan bir İş üzerine çalışma yapmayı planlıyor. Halen İş + TOEIC Programımızda okumaktadır bu program İş Durumlarında İş kelime ve akıcılığını geliştirmesine yardımcı oluyor.Los Angeles\\'ta toplam altı hafta kalacak.\n                    “Los Angeles\\'ı seviyorum. Özellikle Amerikan halkının zihniyetini seviyorum. İş ve fırsatlar hakkında farklı düşünüyorlar. Buradaki insanlar da yeni fikirlere ve bir şeyler yapmaya çok açıklar ve dünyadaki farklı yerlerden pek çok insan var, bu da çok ilginç. Ayrıca plajları da seviyorum. Venice plajı harikadır çünkü serin bir atmosfere sahiptir . Bir Fransız rap şarkıcısıyım. Boş zamanlarımda, Fransa\\'da yaptığım gibi online poker oynuyorum, ama aynı zamanda turist olmak için çok zaman harcıyorum. Çok farklı yerleri ziyaret etmeyi çok seviyorum. Ben de burada spor yapıyorum, tenis ve ağırlık kaldırma gibi. Westwood mahallesi (MLI\\'nın bulunduğu yer) harika bir mahalle ve yaşadığım mahalledir. Diğer birçok ülkeden öğrencilerle tanışmaktan çok mutluyum. İş sınıfımda, beş farklı milletten öğrenci var. Farklı kültürler hakkında bilgi edinmek ve iş hakkında çok şey öğrenmek çok ilginç. Sınıf benim için çok iyi. Öğrencilerin Los Angeles\\'ta İngilizce öğrenmeye gelmesi kesinlikle buna değer. Öğrenciler İngilizce\\'yi veya İş Programı gibi belirli programları öğrenmek istiyorlarsa, bu çok iyi bir fırsat. İngilizcem kesinlikle daha iyi oluyor. İngilizcelerini geliştirmek isteyen her öğrencinin buraya gelmesini öneriyorum! ”"},{id:75,image:"1678977491-1628061377-maria.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:d,title:"MLI Böyle İyi Bir ESL Okulu Yapan Nedir",text:"Bu hafta öne çıkan öğrenci Maria. Kolombiyalı bir TOEFL Akşam öğrencisi. ABD\\'de yaklaşık iki yıl yaşadı. Boş zamanlarında seyahat etmeyi sever. Son zamanlarda tüm Kaliforniya\\'yı görmeye çalışmış ve özellikle Santa Barbara ve Solvang\\'ı sevmiştir. O da bir köpek aşığı!\n\n                    “Bence MLI Los Angeles\\'ta okumak için harika bir yer. Öğretmenler en iyileri. TOEFL öğretmenim Lindsay, çok fazla enerjiye sahip ve öğrencileri derse gelmeye motive ediyor ve bize çalışmamıza ilham veriyor. Ayrıca, buradaki ön personel, tüm öğrencilerin sorularını gerçekten hızlı bir şekilde yanıtlıyor. MLI\\'daki herkes süper dost canlısı ve aynı zamanda eğlenceli bir okul. Farklı bir ESL okuluna gittim ve daha soğuk bir atmosfer vardı ve sadece sistematik değildi, hiç de eğlenceli değildi. Burada arkadaş edinebilirsin. Derse girdiğinizde, sadece iyi ve olumlu hissedebilirsin. Bu kadar eğlenceli hale getirmek için çok fazla alan gezileri ve aktiviteler var. TOEFL sınıfımda da kesinlikle geliştirdim. Konuşmam tonlarca gelisti ve konuşmama güvendigimi söyleyebilirim. Ayrıca çok daha fazla kelime biliyorum ve yazım daha iyi. Plajlar yüzünden Los Angeles\\'ı çok seviyorum. Benim favorilerim Long Beach ve Huntington Beach. Los Angeles\\'taki insanlar çok güzel ve insanlara çok dostça davranıyorlar. New York\\'ta yaşadım ve ilk başta New York\\'u tercih ettim, ama şimdi Los Angeles\\'ı hava durumu, insanlar ve buradaki fırsatlar yüzünden daha çok seviyorum. Bu hafta sonu TOEFL sınavımı alıyorum ve Pazarlama eğitimi için UCLA Extension\\'a geçmeyi planlıyorum. ”"},{id:74,image:"1678977434-1628063174-kaito-1.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:c,title:"Kaito - Japan",text:"Hollywood Kampüsü Öne çıkan Öğrencisi\n\n                    Kaito, Sendai, Japonya\\'dan. O bir break dansçı ve işadamı. 7 aydır Los Angeles\\'ta yaşıyor ve MLI Hollywood\\'da hem ESL hem de Konuşma dersleri aldı.\n                    “Ocak ayında baslangic 1 sınıfında başladım. Temel grammari \"am\", \"is\", \"are\" gibi basit seyleri bile bilmiyordum. Nasıl konuşacağımı bilmiyordum ve başkalarını anlayamıyordum. Yeni başlayanlar sınıfını sevdim çünkü iyi öğretmenleri vardı. Onları anlayabildim. Dersten zevk aldım. Öğrenciler farklı ülkelerden gelmişlerdi onlarla Arkadaş oldum.\n                    2 ay önce Conversation Intermediate programına geçtim. Arkadaşlarımla şimdi konuştuğumda, “İngilizcen çok daha iyi” diyorlar. Ben de hissediyorum. Şimdi İngilizce anlayabiliyorum ve biraz konuşabiliyorum.\n                    Okuldan sonra hip hop müziğini ve gangster rapini “Dogg Pound” ve “South Central Cartel” gibi tarzlari dinlemeyi severim.\n                    Konuşma Programı\\'nı tavsiye ederim çünkü çok fazla konuşma ve dinleme alıştırması yapıyorsunuz. Ayrıca yardımcı olan deyimleri de öğreniyorsunuz. Son tavsiyem, İngilizce konuşmak için utangaç olmayın! \""},{id:73,image:"1678977378-1628063831-mohammed.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:g,title:"Neden MLI\\'da okumalısın ?",text:"Westwood Kampüsü Öne çıkan Öğrencisi\n\n                    Bu haftanın seçkin öğrencisi Suudi Arabistan\\'dan Muhammed. Şu anda Intermediate 1 ESL programımızda okuyor. 2014\\'ten bu yana her yaz Temmuz ayında Los Angeles\\'ı ziyaret ediyor ve Los Angeles hakkında her şeyi çok seviyor. Özellikle oyunculuk hakkinda kendini gelistiriyor. Geçenlerde ilk kez sörf yapmayı öğrenmek için Los Angeles\\'ta bir sörf okuluna kaydoldu. Bu sayede sörfün yakında hobilerinden biri olmasını umuyor! Los Angeles\\'taki en gözde mekanları arasında tüm plajlar Santa Monica, Venice ve mutlak favorisi Malibu yer alıyor.\n                    \n                    “Mentor Dil Okulu\\'nda Los Angeles\\'ta İngilizce eğitimi almanızı öneririm. Bu okul çok iyi bir ESL okulu. Popüler bir üniversiteye (UCLA) yakın olan Westwood, iyi bir bölgede. Bu alanın benim ülkemdeki Suudi Arabistan\\'a benzer şekilde olduğunu hissediyorum. MLI tüm okul personeli ile iyi bir okul! Lindsay (Program Koordinatörü) ve Rafa (Ofis Müdürü) okulun en iyi parçalaridir. Tüm öğrenciler için her zaman çok nazik ve yardımseverler. Bu okulla ilgili her şeyi seviyorum . Öğrencilerin gelip çalışmayı ve çok şey öğrenmelerini öneriyorum.\n                    \n                    Japonya ve İspanya\\'dan öğrenciler gibi birçok farklı uluslararası öğrenciden de farkli kulturler öğrenebilirsiniz. Oyunculuk yapmayı seviyorum ama gelecekteki hayallerim Los Angeles\\'ta bir aktör olmak. Bunun için birçok fırsat var ama ilk olarak ingilicemi gelistirmem gerekiyor ve MLI bunun icin en iyi okul ve secenek.\n                    \n                    öğrencilerin Los Angeles\\'ta mutlaka okuması ve bu deneyimi tatmalari gerekiyor !"},{id:68,image:"1678977059-1628068497-nanami.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:c,title:"Los Angeles\\'ta yapılacak en iyi şeyler",text:"Bu haftanın öğrencisi Nanami. O Japonya Nagoya\\'dan ve yedi aydir Los Angeles\\'ta yaşıyor. Halen H. Intermediate ESL programında. Boş zamanlarında, Los Angeles\\'ta gezmekden yemek ya da alışveriş yapmak için yeni yerler bulmakdan hoslaniyor.\n\n                    \"Los Angeles\\'ı çok seviyorum. Hava çok güzel ve gezilecek birçok yer var. Benim en sevdiğim yer Santa Monica. Orada çok fazla insan var ve herkes çok eğlenceli görünüyor. Ziyaret etmek için en sevdiğim plaj Malibu. Westwood\\'daki okula yakın birçok restorana bayılıyorum. En sevdiğim yer, okulun hemen yanındaki PokeMe! Ayrıca 800 Derece Pizza ve In-N-Out seviyorum. In-N-Out yemek için tipik bir Kaliforniya restorani! En sevdiğim dükkanlar makyaj malzemesi satın almak için Sephora ve giysi almak için Brandy Melville. Westwood yurtunda yaşıyorum, çünkü yeni insanlarla tanışmak çok kolay. Orada yaşadığım zaman asla yalnız kalmıyorum, ki bu da kendime bir daireyi kiralamaktan çok daha mantikli geliyor. Her gün oda arkadaşlarımla konuşabilir ve İngilizce konuşma becerilerimi gelistirebilirim. Okuldan sadece on beş dakikalık bir yürüyüş mesafesinde, bu yüzden çok uygun. Öğretmenlerden dolayı Mentor Dil Enstitüsü\\'nden cok memnunum. Sahip olduğum tüm öğretmenler çok iyi bu okulun en iyi kısmı öğretmenler. Onlar gerçekten eğlenceli çok kibar ve komikler. Sınıflarını almayı ve MLI\\'da okumanızı kesinlikle tavsiye ederim! \""},{id:67,image:"1678976961-1628069001-vaclav.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:d,title:"Vaclav - Czech Republic",text:"Hollywood Kampüsü Öne çıkan Öğrencisi\n\n                    Vaclav, Çek Cumhuriyeti'nden (Prag'a 100 kilometre). Geçen sene liseden mezun oldu. Amerika'ya gelmek her zaman onun hayali olmuştu. Şu anda MLI Hollywood'da Yüksek Orta Düzey programında İngilizce egitimi gormekdedir.\n                    \"Amerika'daki ilk haftalar benim için gerçekten çok zordu. Kendine güvenen, popüler, konuşkan biriyim. Ama Amerika'da tamamen bu farklı oldu. Utangaç, farklı ve insanlarla konuşmakdan ve bir yerlere gitmek korktum. Bu duyguları daha önce hiç hissetmemiştim. Babam İngilizce okuluna başlamami önerdi ve diğer insanlarla birlikte olmak ve İngilizce konuşabilmek için iyi bir fikir olduğunu düşündü. Mentor Dil Enstitüsü'nü bulana kadar bir cok okul aradım. Bu okul benim konaklama yakın bir yerde ve diğer okullardan çok daha ucuz.\n                    \n                    İlk günden itibaren doğru okulu seçtiğimi biliyordum. MLI'da çok fazla kişisel ilgi görüyorsunuz. Sınıflar küçük ve öğretmenler her bir öğrenciye odaklanıyor; Bu sevdiğim ve takdir ettiğim birşey. Kendimi daha iyi hissetmeye başladım çünkü dünyanın farklı yerlerinden insanlarla iletişim kurmanın zor olmadığını fark ettim. MLI'ye gelmeden önce İngilizce konuşanlari anlamak zordu. Komik, çünkü ingilizcemin oldukça iyi olduğunu düşündüm, ama İngilizce konuşanların hızlı konuşması ve bilmediğim deyimler ve argo kullanmalariydi.\n                    Fakat MLI'da öğretmenler açık bir dille konuştular ve anlayabileceğim kelimeler kullandılar. Bu bana güven verdi ve ben de okul dışındaki insanlarla konuşmaya başladım. Hollywood , Griffith Gözlemevi, Santa Monica İskelesi ve daha fazlası gibi farklı yerlere gitmeye başladım. MLI'da başarıya dair tavsiyem korkmuş olsanız bile, kendinizi itin ve KENDINIZ GİBİ KONUŞUN! Hata yapmaktan korkmayin , ve son olarak, seyahat etmek yaşamaktır. Öyleyse gidin ve dünyayı keşfedin! \""},{id:66,image:"1678975220-1628147114-Oguz.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:n,title:"You can achieve all your dreams here.(Oguz | Turkish)",text:"What classes are you taking at MLI?\n                    - I started in High Intermediate ESL, and then moved to Advanced ESL, and now I’m in the TOEFL program.\n                    \n                    Why did you choose to come to study in Los Angeles?\n                    - I came to stay in Virginia last year and while staying there, I took a three day trip to LA. Three days was not enough time here! So, I said to myself, “One day I’m going to live here!” And here I am. It’s a great place to live; the weather is perfect.\n                    \n                    How did you choose MLI?\n                    - One of my friends who lived here in LA said there was this wonderful, amazing language school she went to. She said all the teachers, managers, and students at the school were so kind, and being kind is such an important thing for me. She was talking about MLI. So, I decided to come to the school she recommended, and here I am!\n                    \n                    What are your favorite things to do in Los Angeles?\n                    - I have fallen in LOVE with acting here. I have been in many student films and take classes to improve my acting. I also love discovering new places day-by-day. There are just so many places to discover in LA, it’s never boring.\n                    \n                    Where do you live in Los Angeles? Would you recommend it to other students?\n                    - I live in Westwood. I’m very close to campus in the school dorms. They are good for me because I can meet lots of people. Living there has helped improve my acting- one of my roommates is a director and the other is a cinematographer. There are so many students in Westwood, so wherever you walk, there’s always good, young people around.\n                    \n                    Do you think your English has improved since moving here?\n                    - Of course! I didn’t imagine that my English could get THIS good thanks to the whole crew at MLI. All the teachers and front staff always understand and help to make my English better.\n                    \n                    Do you have any tips for future students?\n                    - If you have dreams for your future, you can be the best of everything here. For example, you can be the best dancer, the best actor, or get the best film experience here. All the best schools and teachers are in LA. It’s the most well-known city in the world, so there are so many professional people in every sector. Don’t be afraid, you can achieve all your dreams while you live here."},{id:65,image:"1678974941-1628147349-Emily.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:e,title:"Do your best and speak in English!(Emily | Taiwan)",text:"What program are you in?\n                    - I'm in the ESL Program.\n                    \n                    Why did you decide to study in in LA?\n                    - I love it in California! Hollywood is a super convenient location and there’s great sunshine all the time!\n                    \n                    Why did you decide on MLI?\n                    - MLI’s tuition is cheap and teachers are great! I searched a lot of schools online and I spoke to agents in Taiwan. Haiwei, is the office manager at Hollywood and he is very helpful.\n                    \n                    How was your English before taking class?\n                    - My English was really bad. I couldn’t understand anything. I couldn’t even order a coffee or go to the supermarket. I wanted to ask questions, but didn’t have the words.\n                    \n                    Has your English improved?\n                    - Yes! Now I can understand English speakers. I can talk and ask questions too.\n                    \n                    Any tips for students?\n                    - Enjoy your time as a student. Do your best and speak in English!"},{id:64,image:"1678974444-1628147734-Fumiya.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:c,title:"Good Location! (Fumiya | Japan)",text:"Studied BEG 2 at MLI WESTWOOD\n                    The staff here at MLI are super friendly and very helpful. The school location is great too. It’s in Westwood so there are many cool places to visit and many stores to shop at! My teachers are always helpful and take the time to explain all my questions to me. I also like that there is a variety of students here so I have a chance to make friends from all over the world."},{id:61,image:"1678968535-1628148128-Martin.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:d,title:"I could improve my English fast (Martin | Czech Republic)",text:"Studied INT 2 at MLI HOLLYWOOD\n                    I came to Los Angeles to learn English and I am so happy I found Mentor. The school is amazing and the teachers are great. I was only here for a month, but I learned more than I ever thought I would. Thank you!!\n                    \n                    And I also felt MLI have great programs too. I started to study from Beginner 1 ESL class. My teachers were realy good at teaching so I could improve my English fast. That motivated me a lot. I\\'m thinking to take TOEFL® class at MLI. MLI will give me the skills to go to university in the U.S."},{id:60,image:"1678968363-1628148669-Victor.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:f,title:"MLI gives me the English skills needed to attend a university in U.S. (Joao Victor | Brazil)",text:"Studied HINT 2 at MLI WESTWOOD\n                    I like MLI for many reasons, first is the location, it is in California so the weather is always good and it is a beautiful place to be.\n                    \n                    Second, I feel the programs here are very good, I started at the beginning level and because my teachers are great, I moved up and improved my English very quickly. I plan on taking the TOEFL® here as well, and I know MLI will give me the English skills needed to attend a university in America which is my dream!"},{id:59,image:"1678968189-1628148897-hani.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:g,title:"I could prepare myself for graduate school by taking the GRE\u002FGMAT course. (Hani |Saudi Arabia)",text:"Studied GRE \u002F GMAT at MLI WESTWOOD\n                    The first day I arrived at MLI they were very welcoming and kind to me.\n                    I felt happy that I chose this school to improve my English and to prepare myself for graduate school by taking the GRE®\u002FGMAT® course.\n                    The teachers and staff are very friendly and I would recommend this school to anyone very highly.\n                    Thank you so much!"},{id:58,image:"1678965970-1628149121-Maria2.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:d,title:"I could made many friends here (Maria | Venezuela)",text:"Studied INT 1 at MLI WESTWOOD\n                    Mentor Language institute is a good school with a great reputation.\n                    Staff members are very kind and helpful and I found no problems while I was here which was wonderful.\n                    The teachers are also very helpful as well and they helped alleviate my shyness when I first arrived.\n                    They also encouraged me to ask many questions which helped improve my English.\n                    I made many friends here thanks to the wonderful staff and teachers and I am so thankful for that."},{id:48,image:"1628149365-Saori.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:c,title:"Come have a blast with us and at the same time improve your English skills. (Saori | Japan)",text:"Studied CONV ADV at MLI HOLLYWOOD\n                    I’ve been studying at MLI, which is located in Hollywood for a year and five months.\n                    During this time, I’ve gone through many things and had many good experiences, more than I ever imagined. I’m really glad that I came to MLI.\n                    \n                    When I first came here, I couldn’t speak English at all, but now I can feel improvements in my English skills, because of teachers and friends I met at MLI.\n                    The teachers always help me and teach me English until I can understand clearly.\n                    They don’t teach me only English, but also culture in the US. In addition, they’re very friendly. Also the staff always helps me when I have questions.\n                    \n                    Another reason that I like MLI is that each level has small class sizes, which means it’s easy to make friends.\n                    There are many students that are from different countries.\n                    If I hadn’t come to MLI, I wouldn’t have learned about different cultures and met people from around the world.\n                    It made me do a complete 180 in my life.\n                    If the school had been boring, I wouldn’t have been satisfied in my life in LA.\n                    It’s a pleasure to have met all the people I met here.If you hesitate to come to LA, I would say “Just do it!!”\n                    Come have a blast with us and at the same time improve your English skills."},{id:40,image:"1628146867-Sofia.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:i,title:"I can really tell I am speaking better than before.(Sofia | Russia)",text:"What program are you in?\n                    - I’m in the TOEFL evening program. I am planning to apply for UCLA extension courses in the future and need a TOEFL score. I want to continue to study in Los Angeles after here to improve my skills in this class.\n                    \n                    Why did you decide to come to Los Angeles?\n                    - I just love California. The weather is so perfect here. LA is really the best place to have a variety of culture. Also, there’s nature everywhere and so much to do. LA is like NYC, but warm!\n                    \n                    Where do you live in LA? Would you recommend it to new students?\n                    - I live in Bel Air and I love it! I think it’s a perfect place to live. The neighborhood is expensive, but I just rent a room in a big house and it’s wonderful.\n                    \n                    What kind of activities do you like to do in LA?\n                    - I LOVE the ocean and surfing. It’s awesome that you can see the ocean and then just drive 2 hours and go snow skiing, or go to the many state parks to bike. If you are addicted to sports, you can find everything here!\n                    \n                    How did you choose MLI?\n                    - I actually spent a month trying a lot of different schools, you know, shopping around LA trying to find the best school for me and then I found MLI. It great quality and price, it’s perfect for me.\n                    \n                    Do you feel your English has improved since coming to LA?\n                    - Absolutely! I have just been at the school about two weeks now and have been reminded of many things I had forgotten from school, and learned a lot of new things- especially vocab. I can really tell I am speaking better than before."},{id:39,image:"1628146649-marina.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:c,title:"I was able to make a lot of close friends.(Marina | Japan)",text:"The reason of Study Abroad・Background・Goals\n                    - When I was in elementary school, my mother used to watch American movies and I often joined her. That made me be interested in American culture. I wanted to go to the States to learn more about the culture. I went to the United Kingdom for a short-term study abroad program while I was in high school, and this experience made me want to stay abroad longer so that I could learn the culture even more. This is why I decided to come to Los Angeles to study.\n                    \n                    Why did you choose MLI?\n                    - I first talked with a study abroad agent about my requests for location, priority and my English skills. My agent picked some schools for me. To select the right school for me, I cared about the quality and cost, and there was only MLI left on my list.\n                    \n                    What were you worried or concerned about before coming to LA?\n                    - I worried about my English ability since I had been feeling like I was the only one who could not understand anything at the school in the United Kingdom. While other students spoke English fluently, I could not. In addition, I have always heard from social media that LA is way more dangerous than Japan, so I was afraid something scary would happen in LA.\n                    \n                    One word to explain MLI\n                    - Teachers and staff at MLI are so nice and kind to me. I was able to say my opinions and ask some questions. It was not only about school, but they also gave me recommendations about good spots in LA and some tips for living in LA. There were also Japanese students at the school, so we all have helped each other when we needed, like sharing information and helping with homework.\n                    \n                    How were your studies at MLI?\n                    - I started from the Beginner class because I was not good at English at all, but teachers were always trying so hard to understand what I wanted to say. In my class we covered speaking, reading and grammar. I felt that Japanese people have strength in grammar but not much in speaking.\n                    \n                    What did you think about the school’s amenities and location?\n                    - I thought the school was so clean and organized. Classrooms, student lounge and restroom were kept clean all the time. Computers, vending machine, refrigerator, microwave, and cooler were provided for all students in the student lounge, so students were able to enjoy their break time there. In addition, MLI is located in a perfect place with sightseeing spots and many kinds of restaurants. As a student I was able to go sightseeing after school and learn about different cultures at various restaurants.\n                    \n                    What do you like to do in your free time?\n                    - There are interesting activities at MLI; Christmas party, Thanksgiving party, Valentine's day and Graduation party for example. At the Halloween party, students, teachers and staff wore high quality costumes to just have fun. There is Santa Monica Beach near MLI, so I often go there on weekends. The weather is so nice in LA, so I take a walk by the beach and get sunburned to feel “California”.\n                    \n                    What was difficult in LA?\n                    - I was confused and had a hard time getting used to going to supermarkets and taking buses and the subway because they were totally different from Japan. What made me feel disappointed was the fact that I could not speak English fluently when I needed someone’s help. That made me not want to go out sometimes. It did not happen to me, but some students even felt home-sick and missed Japanese food a lot.\n                    \n                    Any special episode while you were in LA?\n                    - The culture of lady first, period. I was so impressed that men open the door for women every time when getting in a car. What I was impressed the most was when a waiter at a restaurant was going to refill water for a man, he realized there was an empty glass for a lady and he stopped serving the man and started serving the lady first. It would never happen in Japan. As women, I was so impressed, but I do not know how men would think.\n                    \n                    How is your English improved after coming to LA?\n                    - While I was in LA, a friend of mine came to see me. When we went shopping and sightseeing together, I was translating everything to her and she said she was proud of me because of it. This was the moment I finally felt my English had been improved since I did not have confidence about it. Her words still mean a lot to me.\n                    \n                    What did you earn other than English?\n                    - Friends. I tried to make friendships with foreigners so that I could speak English daily. I was able to make a lot of close friends in the end. None of us could speak English fluently, but we spent time together going shopping, having lunches and partying, and we just had a lot of fun. They mean a lot to me, and I cannot imagine my life without them now."},{id:38,image:"1628146419-Anastasiia.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:i,title:"I’m getting better and better at speaking every day!(Anastasiia | Russia)",text:"What program are you in?\n                    - I’m in the ESL program, Int 2, because I wanted to learn general English skills. I really like the program. The books are great and they help me learn.\n                    \n                    Why did you choose MLI?\n                    - I picked MLI because LA is the center of the world. Hollywood is the center of California and MLI is the center of Hollywood.\n                    \n                    What do you like to do in your free time?\n                    - I like nature, so I go to the beach and hiking a lot. I meet interesting people everywhere because the most interesting people in the world come to LA with a dream to change the world. This makes LA so special and amazing.\n                    \n                    What have you learned living in LA?\n                    - I’ve had many experiences here that have made me more mature and stronger.\n                    \n                    Has your English improved since living here?\n                    - Yes! I’ve been here 6 months and I have seen big progress. I started in Beginner and now I’m in Intermediate 2. I can understand everyone now and I’m getting better and better at speaking every day!"},{id:37,image:"1628146224-Miki3.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:c,title:"My TOEIC score has been improving already.(Miki | Westwood)",text:"This is my third year as a full time employee. After graduating from university, I worked in the wedding industry as a stylist and a make-up artist for two and a half years. However, I majored in biology and chemistry, a completely different field from customer service. While in university, I was interested in studying abroad, but my parents disagreed with it because I did not have a clear reason for it. I gave up on this dream. After years of work experience, I became more interested in religions, cultures and languages, so I left my previous job, and 4 years later, I came to Los Angeles to study.\n\n                    What did you do before coming to LA?\n                    In my first year at a wedding company, I worked in Ginza, where Japanese people and foreigners come to plan their weddings. However, I wasn’t able to communicate well with guests because of my English. Because of this experience, I started learning English seriously. I actually applied for a position at an airline company last summer, but unfortunately I was not accepted. I had promised myself that I would go to the States if I was not accepted this time. All of the international companies in Japan require high English skills, so I was always forced to give up on companies I wished to apply to because of my poor English. Through a study abroad experience, I wanted to learn the language in a country where I could get involved in many cultures, and I would be able to put myself in challenging tasks later.\n                    \n                    Why did you choose MLI? What kind of school were you looking for?\n                    When I was applying for positions at airline companies in Japan, they required a TOEIC score to prove my English ability. I had been struggling in improving my score, so I ended up going to a school that only focused and specialized in TOEIC for three months. This school has the same teaching strategy as MLI. The school I attended in Japan fit me well, but MLI also has ESL, conversation, Business English, TOEIC, TOEFL and IELTS. I chose MLI so that I could take advantage of all the programs. In addition, I was really anxious about going to the States, so it was a relief when I found out MLI had Japanese staff.\n                    \n                    How is your experience at MLI?\n                    I thought studying abroad would be more difficult and feel like something different, but I felt at home all the time in LA thanks to MLI. All the students came to LA with their struggles, but they also came with a passion to improve their English, and there are no differences between ages or nationalities. I am taking ESL class in the morning and conversation class in the afternoon, so I am usually at school for the whole day. (LOL) There are many Japanese students in the morning class, but few in afternoon and evening class. If you wish to take a class which does not have a lot of Japanese students, you can arrange your class the way you want, and this is one of the advantages to studying at MLI.\n                    \n                    How do you like MLI’s location?\n                    MLI is so clean, and surrounded by many restaurants, cafes, CVS pharmacy and banks, so you can live comfortably without any issues. My friend, who studies abroad, used to tell me that it is so inconvenient to live in the states without a car. Now, we have Uber and Lyft which are like cheaper versions of Japanese cabs, Bird (Scooters), Metro Buses and subways as transportation. I have never had problems with transportation here, and there are Japanese supermarkets near MLI so I can cook Japanese foods, too.\n                    \n                    How do you spend your free time?\n                    I used to live in a school dormitory for three weeks, and now I am living in a shared house with an American, Korean, German and Iranian. They speak English fluently, so they motivate me a lot. They always come to me and say \"Miki, let's practice!\", and they teach me English by speaking, watching movies together at night, and hanging out. My Korean roommate and I went to San Clemente State Beach together, and we had a lot of fun. When I am alone, I often go to the gym or cafe to read books or study.\n                    \n                    Has anything interesting happened to you in LA?\n                    After 2 weeks in LA, my wallet and passport were stolen, and this was especially shocking to me. I went out with Japanese friends to a crowded place, and someone opened my backpack and stole my belongings. I really had no idea what had just happened and was so worried that I could ever go back to Japan. Even though I just arrived 2 weeks ago and could not speak English at all, I had to go to the Police department alone and file a report to get a new passport and credit card. This experience was the hardest thing that ever happened to me in my life. However, I was able to grow and learn to overcome these difficulties thanks to this experience. Please be careful and pay attention to your belongings at all times! (LOL)\n                    \n                    How has your English improved since studying abroad?\n                    Although it has only been three months since I came to LA, I do not have any problems with daily conversation now. However, it is still a little hard for me to say my opinions when we learn political science and cultures in class. I have been taking TOEIC class for two and a half months, and my score has been improving already. My weakness is still in reading, so I am trying to read books as much as I can. I often go to cafes near my home and talk with neighbors and baristas, and I really enjoy my time there. Talking to strangers in public places, I know this would not happen in Japan, right?\n                    \n                    What did you earn other than English?\n                    Making friends all over the world is important to me. I had never thought I was able to make friends internationally. I promised my international friends that when I become a flight attendant, I would visit them when I fly to their countries. I would like to apply for an internship later so that I can learn practical English that is really used in the workplace. After that, I will go back to Japan and apply to airline companies one more time. Compared to last year, I have improved my English and experiences abroad, and this will definitely have a positive effect on applying to international companies, so I am going to enjoy my life in LA every single day.\n                    \n                    Would you recommend MLI to future students?\n                    I want to recommend MLI to those who wish to experience something new. The age range is between 20 to 30 years old, so many people can fit and feel comfortable here. An activity is held every Friday, so everyone can go sightseeing and have a lot of fun even without speaking English fluently. I understand that everyone has a different reason for coming to LA, and Westwood campus is located in the perfect area, so it is possible for you to study and visit famous places at the same time. I will definitely recommend it to people like myself who think education is most important, because you can choose the right program from various classes and options. There are also libraries, cafes, and UCLA near MLI so it is easy to connect with other students. But you know, it is all up to you to make a change.\n                    \n                    Any comments for MLI?\n                    Not much. If I must say something... I wish I could have larger desk, but that's it. The Japanese staff is so kind. They support students all the time, so you do not have to worry about living in the States alone. Students tend to come to LA during their Spring or Summer vacation, so there may be a lot of Japanese students during those times, and you may hear Japanese being spoken at school too. Even though MLI has a strict English-only policy for its students, it still creates difficulty in studying English.\n                    \n                    Any tips for future students?\n                    All of you have different situations when coming to the States; however, not many students can actually use their study abroad knowledge in their career. It is okay to end your study abroad as a great memory, but it makes your experience much more worthwhile if you set clear goals while in LA. Before coming to LA, my TOEIC score was around 600, and I regretted that I did not study and review in advance. If you wish to improve your English faster, I highly recommend you learn vocabulary and start now. I wish you all the greatest experience in LA!"},{id:36,image:"1628145767-Vanesa.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:d,title:"The people in LA are really nice, so make friends and have fun.(Vanesa | Bolivian)",text:"What class are you in?\n                    - I’m in the ESL program and also take CMAR class to help my pronunciation.\n                    \n                    How did you choose MLI?\n                    - I wanted to study in Los Angeles because California is so beautiful and the weather is good. I looked online at a lot of schools and thought MLI had such a great location and the price was very accessible.\n                    \n                    What do you think are some of the best places to go in LA?\n                    - I enjoy going to the beach- I love Malibu. I also like the museums in Los Angeles, especially LACMA. It has so many different things to see like art, clothes, furniture, paintings.. It’s so huge. There are a lot of good places to go here, LA is a big place.\n                    \n                    How do you think you have grown since moving here?\n                    - I think I’m always learning so much about other cultures. I have definitely become a stronger person. I also can tell that my English is getting a lot better. I am speaking a lot more and understand more when I listen. When I first arrived here, I think my English was really bad, I couldn’t speak well, but now I’m so much better. I am learning more every day.\n                    \n                    What is your typical week like?\n                    - I go to school Monday-Friday morning and then usually go to the gym after school. I usually go every week to explore new places; LA is so huge there are always new things you can see. I like to ride my bike too. I live in Santa Monica, which is a beautiful place to live and always has a lot to do.\n                    \n                    Do you have any tips for students considering moving to LA?\n                    - Tips for studying at MLI- You need to come to class every day- it’s important to never skip class because we learn something new every day. Tips for coming to LA- The weather is always perfect, so take time to enjoy it. Also, the people in LA are really nice, so make friends and have fun."},{id:35,image:"1628145375-Miki.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:c,title:"Study idioms and vocabulary before you come to LA so you have a basis for improving your English.(Miki | Japan)",text:"Why did you decide to study in LA?\n                    - I came to LA three years ago to study acting and improve my pronunciation in English.\n                    \n                    Why did you decide on MLI?\n                    - I decided to study at MLI because it’s a good school and the tuition was cheap.\n                    \n                    Why did you choose the ESL Program?\n                    - I chose the ESL program because I could improve my listening and speaking skills. My ESL teacher corrected my pronunciation which helped me a lot.\n                    \n                    Has your English improved?\n                    - Yes! Before I came to L.A. , I couldn’t speak English. I was a good reader, and knew a lot of vocabulary, but in Japan I had no opportunity to speak in English. I had a bad accent and people couldn’t understand me.\n                    My speaking skills and pronunciation (especially the ‘R’ and ‘L’ sounds) got much better in LA. Now I speak naturally without thinking about structure or grammar.\n                    \n                    How is life in LA?\n                    - Good! I love the weather. Compared to Japan, LA is laidback and relaxed. In japan you must be punctual, but here it isn’t as strict. Life feels more flexible and free here.\n                    \n                    Any tips for students?\n                    - Study idioms and vocabulary before you come to LA so you have a basis for improving your English."},{id:34,image:"1628144869-Lola.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:j,title:"Don’t be afraid to speak with everyone.(Lola | France)",text:"What program are you in?\n                    - ESL, High Intermediate 2\n                    \n                    What do you like to do in your free time?\n                    - I like to dance at Millenium. I’m into hip hop. I like to go to the beach, Santa Monica Pier. I eat out every day at In and Out with friends.\n                    \n                    What’s the best thing about being in LA?\n                    - Dance!\n                    \n                    What’s the best thing about MLI?\n                    - The teachers!\n                    \n                    Has your English improved?\n                    - Yeah. When I came to America I could understand English, but I could not speak. I’m a shy person so I couldn’t speak with Americans. Now, I speak with everyone!\n                    \n                    Any tips for future students?\n                    - Don’t be afraid to speak with everyone."},{id:33,image:"1628144657-Esther.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:h,title:"I chose MLI and I am really satisfied with my choice.(Esther | Korean,Japan)",text:"How did you choose MLI?\n                    - First, I researched online. I saw there were so many schools in Los Angeles, especially in Koreatown. I saw they were cheap in Koreatown, but I heard they weren’t very good schools, so I decided not to go to them. I researched more and found MLI. I read many great reviews online about MLI, and I saw that many of the reviews were Japanese, which I liked because it would help me feel comfortable. Everything I saw about the school looked really good, and I heard Westwood was a great location, so I chose MLI and I am really satisfied with my choice.\n                    \n                    What’s the best thing about MLI?\n                    - I think the teachers and staff are very kind and funny too. Also, there are many different nationalities in the school, so I can learn about many country’s culture, which makes it really interesting. I can compare things with them and think more internationally.\n                    \n                    What do you usually do during your free time?\n                    - I have been volunteering to help out Lindsay, the Program Coordinator at school. I help her organize and handle paperwork. I volunteered so that I could improve my conversation skills and practice using English, and it’s been really helpful. Also, when I’m not at school, I like to just relax at home and go out with my friends to new restaurants or sightseeing.\n                    \n                    What do you like about Los Angeles?\n                    - The weather is always nice. I really like the people here because they always are friendly. If I say “Hi” or anything like that, they always respond kindly and say things like “Have a nice day.” I like that it’s so positive.\n                    \n                    Do you have any tips or recommendations for students considering moving to LA to study at MLI?\n                    - If you want to improve your English quickly, make sure you study a lot, especially vocabulary. Just knowing Grammar isn’t enough to speak English, the vocab is really the hardest part to be able to use when speaking. Also, I heard that it could be hard to live in LA without a car, but I don’t have one and the metro and buses are pretty good here, so it’s not been a problem for me."},{id:32,image:"1628142750-Sandrine.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:j,title:"Come with an empty suitcase, there’s a lot of shopping here.(Sandrine | France)",text:"What’s your program?\n                    - ESL Advanced\n                    \n                    What do you want to tell new students?\n                    - MLI is a great school. It has great teachers. We learn quickly and we learn a lot of things; pronunciation, grammar, how to write paragraphs and how to speak with people outside of school in life. We also learn how to write emails, official documents and resumes.\n                    \n                    What should students know about life in LA?\n                    - Life in LA is very exciting. There’s a lot of things to do and to discover. There is good weather. People are nice. There’s great dance schools. Millenium (in North Hollywood) and ZH (next to the Melrose dormitory) are my favorite dance schools.\n                    \n                    What area is good for living?\n                    - I like Valley Village because it’s cheap and nice. But if you live here, you should have a car to help you get around.\n                    \n                    Tips\n                    - Come with an empty suitcase, there’s a lot of shopping here.\n                    Six Flags is a great amusement park if you like roller coasters and adrenaline rushes."},{id:31,image:"1628140951-Momoka.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:c,title:"There are many UCLA students around always and I feel so influenced by them.(Momoka | Japan)",text:"What do you think of LA and MLI?\n                    - There are lots of fashionable things here- like stores and people. There’s a lot of diversity here which is cool. There are so many international students here which is really good for speaking English during class. The school is very clean and big too- it’s nice.\n                    \n                    What do you like to do for fun?\n                    - I really enjoy volunteering to help out at MLI. I’m also volunteering at an animal shelter on the weekends starting next week. I haven’t been here very long, but I hope to go sightseeing everywhere. Oh! I also love grocery shopping here- haha! I love Trader Joe’s! They have lots of fun and cheap stuff there.\n                    \n                    Where do you live now? Would you recommend it to new students?\n                    - I live in the school dorms now. They are in Westwood really near the school. I recommend them because they are so near to the school and LA’s bus system isn’t always on time. UCLA is also really close so there are many students around always and I feel so influenced by them.\n                    \n                    Any tips for new students?\n                    - I wish I knew more vocabulary before coming so I could speak more here. It’s important to speak a lot, so don’t be shy when it comes to speaking! LA has so many places to shop, so you don’t need to bring very much. Just bring a goal! My goal is to graduate from university in the US. If you don’t have a goal here, you may not be motivated to learn English as well, but a goal will push you."},{id:30,image:"1628139214-Miharu.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:c,title:"If you want to work in the Entertainment industry, come to LA!(Miharu | Japan)",text:"What program are you in?\n                    - ESL-High Intermediate 2.\n                    \n                    Why did you choose the ESL program?\n                    - In Japan, I only studied English in high school so my English wasn't good and I couldn’t speak. The ESL program at MLI is the best for my general English skills-speaking, listening, grammar. I can learn everything in class!\n                    \n                    Why did you come to LA?\n                    - I was a hair and makeup artist in Japan. I decided to come to LA because I wanted to do photo shoots in LA.\n                    \n                    What do you like about living in LA?\n                    - The weather. And there’s tons of sight-seeing like beaches, mountains, museums and more.\n                    \n                    What’s the hardest thing about living in LA?\n                    - I don’t have a car so it’s hard to visit some places.\n                    \n                    What would you recommend to future students?\n                    - LA has a lot of opportunities for people who want to work in the Entertainment industry, so if you want to work in the industry, come to LA! Try to get involved and meet Americans."},{id:29,image:"1628134935-Kaisei.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:c,title:"MLI events can help your social life.(Kaisei | Japan)",text:"What program are you in?\n                    - ESL-Advaned.\n                    \n                    What do you think new students should know before coming to LA?\n                    - When you come to LA, you should go where ever you want, like famous places. My favorite places to visit are beaches, downtown LA, and museums.\n                    \n                    Why do you like LA?\n                    - I like LA because it’s diverse. There’s a mix of cultures. Around my house in Korea town, there are many immigrants. I can hear many languages on the streets like Spanish, Korean etc.\n                    \n                    What do you like about MLI?\n                    - Firstly, I like the teachers. They’re very friendly and they teach well. Brian, my grammar teacher used to live in France and my other teacher, Gabrielle, is from Venice beach but she lived in Chile, so they both have interesting experiences and they understand the challenges of learning a foreign language.\n                    \n                    What’s your advice to future students?\n                    - You should join MLI events! When I first came to MLI there was a Halloween party. I was nervous about it because I didn’t know anyone. But it was a great opportunity to speak in English with classmates and make friends. MLI events can help your social life ( ="},{id:28,image:"1628134661-ella.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:d,title:"Name: Ella Paravyan",text:"Nationality:\n                    German\n                    \n                    What should students know before coming to MLI?\n                    They should know that the teachers are lovely. They are interested in giving you REAL knowledge that you need, not just school stuff. You should know that you will learn how to speak really fast because of the great people here.\n                    Students at MLI, will not only learn English, but get to know different cultures and different types of people.\n                    \n                    What should students know before coming to LA?\n                    LA is always warm. People are very friendly. People from Europe should not be scared when people say, ‘hi’ and ask, ‘how are you?’ or if they get great customer service. That’s the norm here.\n                    \n                    What’s the best thing about living in LA?\n                    The weather. Friendly people. Diversity of nature; there’s beaches, mountains, etc."},{id:27,image:"1628134450-sara.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:m,title:"Name: Sara",text:"Where are you from?\n                    Spain\n                    \n                    What do you think of LA?\n                    LA is a great place. You can find a lot of things to do here in whatever area you want to study or do. LA really has everything. Also, there are so many nationalities here. It’s a very international city, which is great.\n                    \n                    What are some things you like about MLI?\n                    I like the programs. There are so many programs here like TOEFL, Business+TOIEC, Conversation, the ESL program like I am in, or others. The staff and teachers here in general are so happy and fun- it’s always a great environment. The school always has activities prepared too, which is really great for meeting people, especially if you’re shy or if you came to LA alone like I did. It’s an easy and fun way to meet people and have fun.\n                    \n                    Where do you enjoy going during your free time? What kind of activities do you like to do?\n                    I like a lot of places here. I’m a musician, so I really like going to concerts as well as art museums and exhibits. There are a lot of places for that, like the Disney Concert Hall, and museums. Santa Monica and Venice are fun for hanging out, the Downtown Arts District is cool, and Melrose has great secondhand stores. Every place has its own thing going for it, and every place is different. I am always active- I never stop doing things and am constantly busy. I live with and help out with a family, so I get to see so much of LA with them. I am never bored here. I can always find new things, even just on the streets you can find paintings and graffiti.\n                    \n                    Where do you live now? Would you recommend it for new students?\n                    Now I am living in Malibu. It’s really nice and quiet, but pretty far from the city, so I wouldn’t recommend it for students without a car. I love it though because it’s so green and peaceful.\n                    \n                    Do you have an advice for prospective students?\n                    Don’t be shy because normally foreign students are shy at first. Just be yourself and do your best and work to achieve your dreams."},{id:26,image:"1628134197-shoi.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:c,title:"Name: Shoi Tsuchiya",text:"Nationality:\n                    Japanese\n                    \n                    What program are you in?\n                    ESL High Intermediate 1.\n                    \n                    What do you like to do for fun?\n                    I am a dancer. I always take dance classes after school at Millenium dance complex (a famous dance studio in Studio City).\n                    Sometimes I also go shopping. I like Urban Outfitters. It’s also fun to shop at The Grove and Melrose.\n                    What should students know before coming to LA?\n                    Study vocabulary before you move to America. Vocabulary is very important.\n                    If you are a dancer, you should research dance studios before you come.\n                    \n                    Has your English improved?\n                    Yes. I couldn’t speak English when I came here last year. Now I can speak English and I understand most everything.\n                    \n                    Do you like MLI?\n                    Yes, I like MLI. Everyone is very friendly. Also, the school is in a good location if you are a dancer because there are many dance studios in the area."},{id:25,image:"1628133870-hinata.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:c,title:"Name: Hinata",text:"Nationality:\n                    Japanese\n                    \n                    Program:\n                    IELTS\n                    \n                    How long have you been in LA?\n                    What do you think of it?\n                    I have been here more than a year now. I love it here because of the weather, the people, and the fashion.\n                    \n                    Where do you like to go in LA?\n                    I love to go to the beaches-all of them. Also, I like to go to The Grove, the theatre, and shopping.\n                    \n                    What do you think makes MLI different than other ESL schools?\n                    Everyone here is so kind! Everyone knows me. Even if I can’t speak well, they can understand me and correct my mistakes.\n                    \n                    What neighborhood do you live in? Do you recommend it to new students?\n                    Park La Brea- I recommend it. They have everything you need and I can walk everywhere.\n                    \n                    What are you future plans after finishing studying at MLI?\n                    I want to go to UCLA extension. Now I’m a fashion buyer, so I’ll keep doing that. I may study Business and Marketing at UCLA extension.\n                    \n                    Any tips for prospective students?\n                    You should definitely come to LA to study!"},{id:24,image:"1628133568-touda.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:d,title:"Cheapest ESL School in Los Angeles!",text:"Westwood Campus Featured Student\n\n                    This week’s Featured Student is Touda from Morocco. She currently studies in our Advanced Conversation Program during the afternoon. In Morocco, she works as a journalist and takes additional journalism classes here in Los Angeles. In her free time, she likes to hike, go to the beach, and visit Universal Studios. Here’s what she had to say about MLI:\n                    \n                    “I started studying English in Los Angeles at UCLA extension. When I was studying there, I heard about MLI from a classmate. She recommended this school to me, so I came to check it out and decided to study English here. It’s a really good school and the cheapest ESL school in Los Angeles. UCLA extension is $6,500 per semester, which is just three months. That’s so expensive! My mom even joked that I must be a Moroccan princess because my classes there were so expensive. [Three months at MLI is just $1,200 for the afternoon conversation program]. Both schools are really close to each other in Westwood too, which is the neighborhood where I live. I love this neighborhood because it’s very student-centered with lots of international and native university students around. I’m taking the conversation program now, which really helps me improve my speaking skills for everyday life. If you want to improve your speaking, this is the best class to do it. I think if students really want to learn English, they should definitely come to study at MLI because it’s near UCLA, and is the cheapest ESL school in the area! I really love this school.”"},{id:23,image:"1628132640-denis.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:i,title:"The Best ESL School in Los Angeles",text:"This week’s Westwood Campus Featured student is Denis from Russia. He really enjoys living in LA because of the outdoor activities available. He loves mountain biking and was a professional mountain biker in the past. Here in LA, he bikes as a hobby and loves biking from Mulholland Drive to the sea (which usually takes an hour by car, but he can bike it in 15 min!). He also likes skiing in Big Bear and Mammoth Mountain, as well as surfing at Huntington Beach. He currently takes the TOEFL morning program.\n\n                    “At first, I thought LA was so boring and dirty because I just stayed near LAX, but then I started going out more and moved to Santa Monica and I realized that I was wrong; LA is a very big city with many small towns inside. I actually spent about two weeks discovering and testing out different ESL schools in Los Angeles, like Kaplan and some schools in Koreatown. I spent a few days at each school testing out TOEFL lessons. My girlfriend and I really wanted a place that would give us a lot of new knowledge. There are a few reasons why we decided MLI was the best ESL school for us and chose to study here. First, this school was really new. It has really fresh and new facilities. It’s very comfortable to study here- especially compared to schools in Koreatown. Second, I really liked the lessons that I tried. The format of the lessons in TOEFL class is really good- it’s very similar to Russian style. Third, the price is better than other ESL schools in the area. Before choosing MLI, I had heard Kaplan was best schools in Los Angeles, but it was double the price of MLI, and when I tried the TOEFL class there, the quality wasn’t better. My advice for new students is if you really want to succeed, you must choose a class where others want to study and want to get knowledge ASAP. Some schools have students who just want to keep their visas and don’t really want to learn, but at MLI, this is not the case at all. The students here seem to really want to learn.”"},{id:22,image:"1628132309-bruno.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:f,title:"Life in California",text:"This week’s featured student is Bruno from Brazil.\n\n                    In Brazil, Bruno works in Physical Education, running gyms and training physical trainers. Check out what he has to say about life in California.\n                    \n                    “I love Los Angeles because it looks like Rio de Janeiro, just bigger and less dangerous. Los Angeles is a very big city with people from all over the world. There’s always warm, sunny weather and good vibes. In Los Angeles, you can build any lifestyle you want. In my free time I like to work out at Gold’s gym, go to restaurants with friends, go to the beach, and hike. People should visit the Staples Center in downtown L.A. because the best team in the NBA, the Lakers, plays there. Dodger Stadium is a baseball stadium with great energy too. The baseball crowd is like the football crowd in Brazil. I’d also recommend the bar, “Bungalow”, in Santa Monica because it’s outdoors by the beach and the most beautiful people party there. My favorite bar in West Hollywood is Barney’s on Santa Monica Boulevard. They have pool tables, music, and karaoke.\n                    \n                    I live in West Hollywood. It’s really nice there- safe, calm, clean, and there’s a lot to do; bars, restaurants etc. I used to live in Beverly Hills and really liked it there too. There’s a lot of good shopping, like the Grove. Remember, Los Angeles is huge and public transportation is not great. I ride my bike to school. If you can, rent or buy a car. In general, life in Los Angeles is expensive compared to other places in the United States, but worth it.\n                    \n                    I would recommend Los Angeles to everyone!"},{id:21,image:"1628128541-lisa.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:d,title:"How to get 100+ on the TOEFL exam!",text:"Westwood Campus Featured Student\n\n                    This week’s featured student is Lisa from Germany. She recently achieved 108 on her TOEFL test! During her free time she likes to do anything creative from pottery to knitting. She runs a blog in English and also loves cooking and trying new foods in Los Angeles. She recommends that students eat a lot while they’re studying here because the food is so diverse and there are tons of authentic foods here. Her favorite place in Los Angeles is Abbott Kenney in Venice.\n                    \n                    “I was in the TOEFL program for 12 weeks. Before taking the TOEFL class, I studied in the ESL program at MLI. I achieved 108 because I really listened to everything that Kyle [the morning and afternoon TOEFL teacher] had to say. His class is really great for improving your score. After class, I would always review the classroom tasks at home to see what I missed and figure out why I missed it. I think the Purpose\u002FMethod and Vocabulary Questions in the reading are the hardest type of question for me. I think the vocabulary in class was actually harder than on the real test though! I think that for students to really develop their English skills to be able to pass the TOEFL exam, they need to really change their whole private life to English. For example, you have to watch movies in English, participate in small talk in English, and especially think in English. I always think in English now when I’m consciously thinking. I also think Kyle’s Strategy Guide [a book of TOEFL strategies written by the morning\u002Fafternoon TOEFL teacher] is so helpful too- especially the part with the synonym structure. It’s so helpful to know how to change words into synonyms. Also, the speaking practice questions were very helpful- I used the guide a lot to prepare."},{id:20,image:"1628128170-adbulmajeed.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:g,title:"How to go to College in Los Angeles",text:"Jay is from Jeddah, Saudi Arabia. He earned his Bachelor’s degree in Management Hospitality at Prince Sultan University in Jeddah in 2013. In May 2016 he moved to Los Angeles with the hopes of getting his Master’s degree in Food and Catering from a college in the United States. I spoke with Jay this week to learn more about his path to university.\n\n                    “ In 2016 I came to California on a scholarship from my government to improve my English skills and go to college. For international students, colleges in the United States require a TOEFL or EILTS score. This shows the university your English proficiency level. I didn’t know anything about the TOEFL test before I came to America, besides that it was an English test.\n                    \n                    Before I could handle university material, I had to improve my writing skills. I decided to take the ESL program at MLI to work on this. Later, I decided to take the TOEFL class to prepare for the test. I want to get between an 80-90 score, which is high. Northridge College in California requires a score of 84 on the TOEFL test and Pomona college requires a score of 89.\n                    \n                    Now I’ve been in the TOEFL course for 5 months. It is challenging. We focus on test strategies, academic vocabulary, reading comprehension and essay writing. We often need to summarize Academic readings and lectures. The TOEFL course has helped my English skills a lot. I can now summarize and understand the main ideas of a lecture, reading or listening without having to read all the details.\n                    Besides the TOEFL test, I need to take the GMAT test to apply for my Master’s degree. I’m going to study with a private tutor to help me prepare for that. Once I have my TOEFL and GMAT scores, I will apply to Northridge, Pomona and Tampa State University in Florida.\n                    \n                    My advice to future students who want to go to college is, know the college requirements for application BEFORE moving to America. This well help you choose the best English program for you.”"},{id:19,image:"1628127696-alejandra.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:m,title:"A Typical ESL Student’s Schedule",text:"Westwood Campus Featured Student\n\n                    This week’s featured student is Alejandra. She is from Madrid, Spain. In Spain she works in the film and media industry and has worked on big shows like “The Voice: Spain.” During her free time, she likes to play volleyball and see movies.\n                    \n                    “Typically I go to school from Monday to Friday 9-12:50 a.m. [in the Intermediate 2 ESL Program]. After school, I either go back to my apartment to hang or go out with my friends to get to know and explore Los Angeles. I really love going to Melrose Ave for shopping and also going to Santa Monica Beach to play beach volleyball with some of my friends who live here in LA. I also enjoy going to see movies here, which helps me improve my listening skills. On the weekends, I like to take road trips outside of Los Angeles. Los Angeles is near to many different places, like last weekend I went with friends to Arizona on a road trip. We went to Monument Valley and Antelope Canyon! I had a lot of fun and the places were really amazing. I live in Hollywood, which is pretty cool because it has many studios like Netflix and Paramount Pictures, so it’s fun to be around those kinds of things. I think a student should plan to come study in Los Angeles for more than three months to really have a chance to know California. I haven’t had enough time here yet to see everything that I want to see. I’ve really enjoyed Los Angeles, but want more time here than I have. I think MLI is such a nice ESL school because there are lots of different nationalities of international students here. Also, the teachers are very close to each other and are very good. I think it’s really fun too because there are always so many activities!”"},{id:18,image:"1628127256-haruka.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:c,title:"Best Teacher I’ve Ever Had",text:"Hollywood Campus Featured Student\n\n                    This week’s featured student is Haruka Mishiro from Chiba, Japan. She moved to Los Angeles 10 months ago to study English at MLI. After school, Haruka takes dance classes at Millenium and Edge. Jazz funk is her favorite form of dance and she loves to perform. Haruka talked to me today about her classes at MLI and her favorite English teacher.\n                    \n                    “I have been studying at MLI for almost a year. I started in the Beginner 1 class, but now I’m in Intermediate 2. The best teacher I ever had is Lisa. She was my grammar teacher in Beginner 1 and 2. She teaches clearly and slowly so that everyone understands. She’s very patient.\n                    I learned a lot from her. We practiced talking to each other every day in class. On Mondays, we talked about what we did over the weekends. It was helpful because we got to talk and practice grammar in conversation. We also got to learn about our classmates. Sometimes we played grammar games in class, like Bingo. There were 2 teams and we needed to build sentences. For example, we would need to make sentences using the ‘be verb’, ‘going to’, ‘will’, or ‘was’. I liked the games because they were fun and exciting. We all yelled and cheered. We all wanted to win the game and be the best. Lisa helped us with pronunciation too which I liked.\n                    Lisa is so kind. I love Ariel, the Disney character from Little Mermaid, so one day Lisa taught the Beginner class the song, “Part of Your World”. The whole class sang along and it was so much fun. After school me and my friends sang the song again and again. Lisa is a great teacher and she gives the best hugs. Her hugs always make me happy!”"},{id:17,image:"1628126940-chintan.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:d,title:"Student Activities",text:"Hollywood Campus Featured Student\n\n                    Chintan Shah was born and raised in Mumbai, India. He studied IT (Informational Technology) at University and worked as an IT technician for one year. However, Chintan had big dreams of becoming a filmmaker, so he quit his job in India and moved to Los Angeles. For the past four years he’s lived in L.A. working on more than 20 short films and 15 music videos. He currently shoots promotional videos and BTS (behind the scenes) for celebrities’ social media accounts.\n                    \n                    Chintan has been taking the Business\u002FTOEIC Program at MLI Hollywood for the last 6 months in order to improve his Business skills and pronunciation. Chintan always participates in school activities so I spoke with him about his experience.\n                    \n                    “Going to school activities was cool because I met so many different people with different nationalities. It helped grow my cultural awareness and make new friends. I went to Vegas with over 30 different students from both Hollywood and Westwood campus. We went to bars, the club, the strip, and I drank on the streets of Vegas with my classmates. It was amazing! Best time ever!\n                    \n                    I went on a school field trip downtown too. We visited the Broad museum, the Last Bookstore, and we also saw the Grand Central Market, which is one of the best places I’ve ever eaten. My friends ate at Egg Slut and they loved it!\n                    I went to LACMA and the Natural History Museum as well. We played a scavenger hunt at the Natural History Museum where we had to find 13 different exhibits and take a selfie of the exhibit with our team. We were in it to win it. At LACMA I got to see so many different art collections. There were many artists and many cultures represented.\n                    I would recommend participating in school activities as it will be both informative and fun!”"},{id:16,image:"1628125406-cindy.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:f,title:"What it's like to study ESL in Los Angeles",text:"MLI Westwood Featured Student\n\n                    This week’s featured student is Cindy from Brazil. In Brazil, she works as an interior designer and plans to study Architecture at a university here in Los Angeles. She has lived in Los Angeles for 5 months now and really enjoys going to the beaches and clubs here.\n                    \n                    “I’ve been studying English in Los Angeles for about 5 months now. When I first came to MLI, I was surprised because the students here are so serious. I used to go to a different ESL school, but I think MLI is good to learn English because all the students are very serious about learning English. I live in Culver City and I definitely recommend it to students, especially Brazilians, because there are many Brazilians who live there, so it is fun. I also think Westwood [where the campus is located] is a good place to live too because it’s near the school and it’s a good location. In LA, there is so much to do. I love going to the beaches- Venice is my favorite one. I also love going to clubs, because I love dancing. I have many international friends here now, so I love to hang out with them. Typically after class, I often go to the beach, to the gym, to dinner with friends. I also really like the amusement parks in Los Angeles- Universal Studios and Six Flags are cool. There are also many parties for students to get involved in and meet people. I definitely recommend other students to study in Los Angeles. LA is not a cheap place, but I think it’s better than Brazil. I love it here so much! I even got a tattoo of Los Angeles because I feel like I belong here and wish I could live here forever. It really is such a beautiful place. It has great vibes, wonderful people at school, and nice weather. I definitely recommend students to come study English in Los Angeles.”"},{id:15,image:"1628124992-giovanna.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:o,title:"Tips for future students",text:"Westwood Campus Featured Student\n\n                    This week’s featured student is Giovanna from Italy. Giovanna is from the Italian countryside near Venice. She enjoys drawing, photography, modeling, and sewing during her free time. Also, she recently enjoys driving around Los Angeles because she just got her driver’s license last week. She currently takes the TOEFL Evening program.\n                    \n                    “I think it’s important that students don’t speak their native language when studying English in Los Angeles. Even when I’m with Italian people, I always speak English- especially when I’m in front of native English speakers. I think students need to speak as much English as they can. Also, I always translate and understand all the songs I listen to and imitate their singing to work on my pronunciation and always start my day reading the newspaper in English- both about my country’s news and US news. That’s really helpful for vocabulary and just knowing what is going on everywhere. I live in Inglewood now. The rent is very cheap, but some areas are kind of dangerous. I live between Jefferson and Adams and the neighborhood is mostly families around, so it’s totally fine for me. It’s also very near the Farmdale Metro station, so it’s easy to get around Los Angeles. I do think students need to make sure they are always aware of their surroundings and don’t just trust everyone they meet. I love going to the art museums here. There are many free museums, like the Broad, that are pretty cool. I like the Griffith Observatory too. They have this nighttime star show that is really amazing. I think students need to find their own places- not just what they see on Instagram. LA is actually a lot nicer than you see on social media. I really enjoy studying English at MLI. I like that they have evening lessons because I definitely enjoy studying in the evening more than in the morning. Also, the staff and everyone here is really helpful.”"},{id:14,image:"1628124330-yukari.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:e,title:"En büyük tavsiyem; kendine güven!",text:"Yukari Satoe Japonya'dan. Geçen yıl Los Angeles'ta MLI Hollywood'da yaşadi ve ingilizce egitimi gordu. Boya yapmayı, kitap okumayı, yemek pişirmeyi ve dans etmeyi seviyor. Gelecekte dans öğretmeyi ve profesyonel olmayi umuyor.\n\n                    “Kuzey Hollywood'da bir aile yanında yaşıyorum. O evi seçtim, çünkü evi çok sevdim. Okuldan bir arkadaşım olan Nanami, o evde daha once yaşadı ve beni ev sahibine tanıttı. Orada yaşamanın en güzel yanı, binada bir havuz ve caddenin karşısında bir spor salonu olmasi. İngilizce becerilerimi geliştiriyorum çünkü ev sahibi annem Japonca konuşmuyor. Ana dili İngilizce olanlarla pratik yapmak isteyen öğrencilere aile yanında kalmalarini tavsiye ediyorum.\n                    Okuldan sonra resim yapmayı, kitap okumayı, pişirmeyi ve dans etmeyi severiyorum. Jazz funk, hip hop, contemporary, ve heels dans tarzlarini seviyorum . Los Angeles'ta birçok harika dans stüdyosu var. Melrose Avenue'de (Melrose yurduna yakın) Dans alani çok iyi bu yuzden herkes orada dans etmekten hoşlanıyor. Atölye çalışmaları ve özel dans eğitmenleri için sadece Millenium'a gidiyorum. Movement Lifestyle ayrıca Kuzey Hollywood tren istasyonunun yakınında iyi bir dans stüdyosu. Burayı sevdim çünkü cogu insan dans etmeyi seviyor. Gelecekte dans etmeyi öğretmek istiyorum ve harekete geçmek istiyorum. LA'da dans etmekle ilgileniyorsanız, Instagram'a girmenizi, beğendiğiniz bir öğretmeni bulmanızı ve nerede öğrettiklerini öğrenmenizi öneririm. Doğru dans okulunu bulmak için LA'ye gelene kadar beklemene gerek yok.\n                    \n                    En büyük tavsiyem; kendine güven!"},{id:13,image:"1628070618-miki2.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:e,title:"Şimdiye kadar katilacaginiz en iyi sınıf",text:"Westwood Kampüsü Öne çıkan Öğrencisi\n\n                    Bu hafta öne çıkan öğrenci Japonya'dan Miki. Japonya'da bir düğün kutlama şirketi ile çalışıyordu , ancak gelecekte bir uçuş görevlisi olmayı planlıyor. Boş zamanlarında, kahve dükkanına takilmayi ve ders çalışmayı seviyor. Bazen de müzelere gitmekten hoşlanıyor - özellikle ücretsiz ve okulun yakınındaki Hammer müzesine. Westwood'da yaşıyor ve yeni öğrencilere bu bölgeyi tavsiye ediyor.\n                    \n                    “TOEFL sınıfı, sahip olduğum en iyi sınıf. Katıldığım zaman, İngilizce becerilerimin tümünü geliştirebiliyorum - Dinleme, Yazma, Konuşma ve Okuma. Kyle da çok komik bir öğretmen - şakaları her zaman çok ilginç ve eğlenceli. Sınıftaki tüm öğrenciler çok ciddi ve motive. Sınıfta başka Japon öğrenciler olsa da, sadece İngilizce konuşuyorlar, ki bu çok yardımcı oluyor. TOEFL programı, günde bir gün Okuma ve Konuşma, bir sonraki gün Yazma ve Dinleme gibi iki beceriyi gelistirmek ve Pratik yapabilmemiz için oluşturulmuştur. Her ay bir kez TOEFL testleri oluyoruz. Skorum kesinlikle gelişiyor. İlk skorum suan ki skorumdan çok daha düşüktü ve bir sonraki skorumun son seferkinden çok daha yüksek olacağını umuyorum. İngilizcem de kesinlikle gelişiyor. Okulu ve TOEFL sınıfını kesinlikle tavsiye ederim. MLI'ya ilk geldiğimde çok gergin hissettim çünkü hiç İngilizce bilmiyorum ama okul bana çok yardımcı oldu. Amerikan bankası, staj ve daha rahat hissetmek için bir daire bulmama yardımcı oldular. Şimdi çok daha rahat hissediyorum ve LA'yı seviyorum çünkü buradaki insanlar çok kibar ve arkadaş canlısı. ”"},{id:12,image:"1628070274-mertcan-1.jpg",campus_name:a,nationality_name:e,title:"Diger ESL okullarina kiyasla neden MLI’i seçmelisiniz",text:"Westwood Kampüsü Öne çıkan Öğrencisi\n\n                    Bu hafta öne çıkan öğrenci Türkiye'den Mertcan. Şu anda Advanced ESL sınıfında eğitim görüyor. Boş zamanlarında, Venice'de basketbol oynamayı çok seviyor. Oynamaya gittigi gunler yeni tanistigi her cesit insan ile oynayabiliyor. Aynı zamanda boş zamanlarında bilgisayar kodlamasi yapıyor ve sürekli bunun hakkında daha yeni şeyler öğreniyor. Şu anda Mar Vista'da yaşıyor ve yeni gelecek öğrencilere kesinlikle tavsiye ediyor çünkü orası Venice Sahili'ne çok yakın.\n                    \n                    “Los Angeles'ta okumak için bir ESL okulu arayan diğer öğrencilere MLi'i %100 tevsiye ediyorum.\" MLI, bölgedeki diğer ESL okullarına kıyasla en ucuz İngilizce okulu ve kaliteside çok iyi. MLI'yı diğer ESL okullarından daha iyi yapan şey bu. Özellikle öğretmenlerin harika olduğunu düşünüyorum. Öğretmenlerim Sheena ve Barry'nin olumlu bir tutumları var ve çok nazikler. Westwood bölgesini seviyorum. Okul etrafinda ihtiyacınız olan her şeyi bulabilirsiniz, LA Fitness ve UCLA gibi. MLI, bir çok kültürü öğrenebileceğiniz bir çok uluslararası öğrenciye sahip. Çalışırken, sadece öğretmenlerinizi dinleyin ve başkalarının sizi rahatsız etmesine ya da endişelenmenize izin vermeden kendi hedeflerinize odaklanın. Los Angeles, yaşamak için harika bir yer. Yaklaşık 2 yıldır buradayım ve en çok plajları seviyorum. Ziyaret etmek için harika bir yer olan Venice yakınlarında yaşıyorum. Ayrıca Griffith Gözlemevi'nide ziyaret etmek için güzel bir yer olduğunu düşünüyorum. Bence Los Angeles'taki insanlar çok güzel ve yardımsever. Los Angeles’taki kültürü gerçekten çok seviyorum ve kesinlikle burada ingilizce ögrenmek için gelecek uluslararası öğrencilere burayi tavsiye ederim."},{id:11,image:"1628069853-tanice.jpg",campus_name:b,nationality_name:f,title:"Tanice - Brazil",text:"Hollywood Kampüsü Öne çıkan Öğrencisi\n\n                    Tanice Porto Alegre, Brezilya’dan. Bir yıl önce tatile Los Angeles'a geldi. Amerika'ya geldiğinde, ingilizcesinin çok iyi olmadığını fark etti; İngilizcede zorluk çekiyordu, hatta kahve siparişi bile çok zordu. İngilizce becerilerini geliştirmek icin MLI Hollywood'da ingilizce egitimi gormeye karar verdi. Boş zamanlarında plaja gitmeyi, ve ders çalışmayı seviyor. Şu anda Advanced ESL programında egitim goruyor.\n\n                    “Amerika'ya geldiğimde korktum çünkü hiç İngilizce bilmiyordum. Ama korkumun beni durdurmasına izin vermedim. Hata yapsam bile, hep konuşmaya çalıştım. İngilizcemi geliştirmemde bana en cok yardımcı olan şey herkesle konuşmaktı; Uber sürücüleri ve sokaktaki insanlar. Utangaç değilim, böylece her nefes alabilen kişi ile konuşmaya başladım! İngilizcem'e yardımcı olan bir başka şey de sadece Brezilyalıları değil aynı zamanda diğer ülkelerden gelen insanlarla da arkadaş olmak. Kendi ülkenizdeki insanlarla olmak rahattır, ancak İngilizcenizi bu şekilde geliştiremezsiniz.\n\n                    Youtube videoları izleyerek kendimce İngilizce öğrendim ve bunun tonlarca yardimi oldu! En sevdiğim Youtuber'lar “Leila ve Sabrah ile İngilizce” ve “Papa English”. Her zaman yeni videoları var. Cok eğlenceli ve hızlı.\n                    Ben de bazı Brezilyalı ve Amerikan İngilizce öğretmenlerini takip ediyorum. Her gün öğretmenler bir yerli gibi konuşmayla ilgili ipuçları veriyor.\n                    Instagram'da @mariovergara (Portekizce ve İngilizce dilinde İngilizce ipuçları) kontrol etmelisiniz.\n                    Yaptığım bir başka güzel şey de, her gün uyumadan önce ve spor salonunda olduğum zaman Duolingo'yu kullanmaktan hoşlaniyorum. Günlük İngilizce becerilerine yardımcı oluyor. MLI'ya gelmeden önce hiç gramer bilmiyordum. MLI bana sozluk kullanmadan yazmam ve konuşmam için cok yardımcı oldu. ”"}]}],fetch:{},mutations:void 0}}("Westwood Campus","Hollywood Campus","Japanese","Other Nationalities","Chinese","Brazilian","Arabic","Korean","Russian","France","tr","","Spanish","Turkish","Italian","All Campus")));